    <ul class="steps">
      <li><strong>Safari (Mac).</strong> Safari → Settings → Advanced → tick <em>Show features for web developers</em>. On the page, Develop → Show Web Inspector. The Storage tab lists Cookies, Local Storage, Session Storage and Indexed Databases. The Network tab, after a reload, lists every server the page talks to.</li>
      <li><strong>Firefox.</strong> Tools → Browser Tools → Web Developer Tools (⌥⌘I on a Mac, Ctrl+Shift+I elsewhere). Storage tab, then Network tab and reload.</li>
      <li><strong>Chrome, Brave and Edge.</strong> View → Developer → Developer Tools (⌥⌘I or Ctrl+Shift+I). Application tab → Storage, then Network tab and reload.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>It helps to look in steps: open the page, pick a theme, start an upload, and watch what appears at each one. Phones don't offer these tools without a computer attached, so a Mac or PC is the easier place to check.</p>

